{"kind":"assert","text":"For Hugh: give ordinary documentation verification one command with a clear scope. This is a small workflow recommendation for the AGENTS/SKILL simplification work #20305 and its runnable-guide companion #21369. It supplements the existing advice to report evidence accurately; it does not add another approval or completion state.\n\nThe concrete failure: the approved Case C documentation merge 0afa98aa reached main with twenty broken ordinary Markdown links. [CI run 34398581451](https://github.com/generalbusiness-ai/gitseq/actions/runs/34398581451) then failed the existing root [TestLocalMarkdownLinks](public_surface_test.go@0afa98aa26be6756682f28defb081043ecc8efa2:169). Earlier docset/build and native source-window checks had passed; those checks did not cover ordinary Markdown destinations. I independently reproduced the root failure with Go1.26.7; the actual output is attached. The [Makefile documentation target](Makefile@0afa98aa26be6756682f28defb081043ecc8efa2:9) runs only ./internal/docset/..., so invoking make docs does not invoke the root link test. The distinction is easy for both author and reviewer to miss.\n\nRecommendation: have make docs run the existing focused root Markdown-link test first, then the existing docset checks, and use that named recipe wherever the instructions describe ordinary documentation verification. Keep one authoritative explanation of its scope and link to it from the work sequence and walkthrough. This consolidates existing checks; it does not invent a new review stage, relax CI or require the full Go suite for every prose correction. If accepted, assign the small Makefile/documentation outcome explicitly before implementation, rather than silently adding it to the existing editorial-only commission.\n\nState the limits beside the recipe. The [root checker](public_surface_test.go@0afa98aa26be6756682f28defb081043ecc8efa2:197) deliberately skips HTTPS links and checks local file/heading destinations. It cannot prove an external exact-source URL or a native preview interaction. Where a change promises clickable source previews, separately test the actual rendered component and its requested source window. The Case C repair review 73754df5 shows why: its root gate passed while the UI still rendered twenty unavailable markers. A passing API-window request is also not a clicked-link test. Avoid calling any one of these checks complete documentation proof.\n\nThe benefit to test is fewer repeated decisions about which ordinary documentation command to run, and catching this known class of link error before approval. I have not measured delivery-time savings, and one incident does not establish a fleet-wide failure rate. The current CI repair remains assigned and can finish independently; this note is for your review, not an adopted policy or permission to rewrite the existing workflow.","body":{"head":"0afa98aa26be6756682f28defb081043ecc8efa2","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:10d95b2f49445ec183db37edfff722bd29511c67, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:434b97fbe08a57ee73ce17fe4c2d2fdc18b2c58e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:73754df5f59b48e3b9e92a4a99a7fdfcf8408200, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:852f2f757915951e869a855720413c7270572da7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:edfc45a0f514fb6dc3725b7142b752acb27ebbb2 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c819676fead7d19fdd20633b48dc16c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:010aac64d68bdeac36cf6c443ce7305d53a60fe8, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:012451209d3000492d2e523089e5973beec05f61 and 348 more"}}